WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.035
-Our next guest tonight
is a Tony- and Emmy-nominated

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:05.238
and Grammy Award-winning actress
who you know

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.540
from her work on Broadway
in "The Color Purple"

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.909
and "The Piano Lesson."
She reprises the role of Sofia

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.511
in the new movie version
of "The Color Purple,"

00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:14.113
which is in theaters
on Christmas Day.

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.281
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.850
-A pretty girl like you
can take his mind,

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.253
but you can't have his money.
-He ain't got no money.

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:23.589
See, my sister
and her husband say

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.791
I can live with them
as long as I please.

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:30.463
Now, I come here
out of respect.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:35.067
But if there ain't none to get,
there sure ain't none to give.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.403
Don't keep me waitin'.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:39.172
-Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.240
our friend Danielle Brooks,
everybody!

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.676
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.679
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:58.357
♪♪

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:02.728
Now, you -- you, my friend,
are in celebrating clothes.

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.397
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.933
I think, every time I come here,
I get sexier and sexier.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.901
-You do!
-Ooh!

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.202
[ Cheers and applause ]
So do you!

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:11.938
-Oh, my God, thank you
for saying that.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.474
-The hair is popping.
-Thank you very much.

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:18.111
-Yes, we're celebrating.
-You were nominated

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.378
for a Golden Globe.
-Yes.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:21.514
-Nominated just today.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.149
Just today for
a Critics Choice Award.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.651
Congratulations.
-But, you know,

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.051
I got a beef with you.
-What's that?

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:28.721
-First of all, that's a lot
to celebrate -- good stuff.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.691
But I've been on this show
four times now.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.125
-Yeah.
-And I think it's time

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:34.627
we pop a bottle.
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.930
We got a lot to celebrate.
You don't ever have nothing.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.067
Oh! [ Laughs ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:44.304
-Here's to you
and all your successes.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.372
-Thank you!

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.607
Okay!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:51.844
Yeah. Yeah.
That was worth it.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.579
-Was it worth it?
I'm glad you thought

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.014
it was worth it.
-I do, I do.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.118
-This is -- "The Color purple"
is a very exciting film for you.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.618
The first time you were here,
2016, was

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.321
because you were
in the Broadway show.

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.855
-Yes.
-And we talked about

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.156
how cool that was, because
that had been the first --

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:05.791
that was the first Broadway
show you ever saw.

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:08.327
-Yes, first Broadway show
I ever saw.

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:11.197
10 years later,
first Broadway show I star in.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.966
-Wow.
-And now, almost a decade later,

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:16.169
first studio film.
-That's amazing.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.703
-[ Squeals ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.640
Thank y'all.
It's been an amazing ride.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.709
-I mean,
how has your relationship

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:25.010
with the character changed over?
I mean,

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.380
do you feel closer to it,
do you feel like

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.248
you have a different perspective
on it, having done it?

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:31.517
-Oh, definitely different
perspective, deeper perspective.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:34.153
It's really cool because
it's not often that an actor

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:37.957
gets to step into the theater
and do it in film

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.660
with the same character,
so it's been a thrill.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.561
Like, it's been
so, so, so, so cool.

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.964
And getting to bond
with people like Miss Oprah...

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.632
-Yes.
-...and Taraji and Fantasia

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:48.901
and Colman and Corey.
It's been a dream.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.537
-And now this is the role
Oprah played in the film

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:52.906
in the '80s.
-Uh-huh.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.674
-And she's a producer
on this film.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.443
How -- Has she
given you advice or...

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:00.646
-She has given me advice --
a lot of advice.

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.348
But, you know,
the number-one thing is,

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.584
when I got to talk to her
about this character --

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:08.555
finally got the courage to talk
to her about the character --

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:11.924
I actually asked her, in our
hour-and-a-half conversation.

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:13.459
I said, "Can you pray for me?"

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.828
And she did, and I'm so glad
she did, because

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:19.298
you know she got a direct
connection and line to God.

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:21.700
So if you're going to get
anybody to pray for you...

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.369
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-...it better be Oprah Winfrey.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.472
-Oh, my God, that's great.
-My life has changed completely

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.708
[Laughs]
ever since that conversation.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.644
-Yeah. Um, you mentioned
Corey -- Corey Hawkins.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.712
And so he is your costar
in this film,

00:03:33.712 --> 00:03:37.216
and he -- you were classmates
together at Juilliard.

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:38.484
-Yeah.
-So is that first year

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.620
at Juilliard, you meet Corey?
-Oh, my God, yes.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.621
-Wow. So you're kids.
-In 2007, we met.

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:44.657
Isn't that crazy?
We were babies.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.824
-That's amazing.

00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:47.293
-We've been cutting up
ever since.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.129
But he's seen every valley,
hill, mountain.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.764
We've climbed them together.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.500
And so finally we here
in "Color Purple" together.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.903
-And you mentioned cutting up
together for a long time.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.937
And so here you are, you're
in a studio film together.

00:03:58.937 --> 00:04:02.008
And it just must be so surreal,
because, obviously, you know,

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:05.511
this is a work of humor,
but it's also a very heavy film,

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:08.014
and it just must be so nice
to be with a friend

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.548
you've been friends with
for a long time.

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:11.350
And you have a video
you want to share.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.120
Corey maybe ate too much
during...

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.356
-Crafty? He spends
too much time at crafty.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:18.624
-That's at craft services,
where all the food is.

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:21.494
-Yes. Right.
And so after eating too much,

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.863
his pants kept popping on set.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.865
And I just thought it was
the most funniest thing,

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.368
so I had to -- I begged him
to take this video for me.

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.469
-Now, the most fun part
about this video

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.171
is how hard
you're laughing off camera.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.906
[ Laughter ]
And it's nice to know this is

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.474
not the first time
it's happened,

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.576
and you're still laughing
like it's the first time.

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.812
Let's take a look at Corey.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.948 line:50%
Wait. Okay.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:45.051 line:50%
[ Both laughing ]

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:48.421 size:88% position:44% line:50%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:51.557
-Oh, my God! I love it.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:54.127
Like, people who don't
take themselves too seriously.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.594
-I know.
-You know what I mean?

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:57.130
And now he's, like,
running a marathon.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.131
So he's all skinny and slim now.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:59.131 --> 00:05:00.799
Oh, that's very nice of you
to point that out, as well.

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:02.468
-I had to look out for him.
-He stopped.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.503
He's going the other direction.
-Yeah, other direction.

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:07.106
Can I -- Your daughter, Freeya,
is four years old.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.674
-Yes.
-Here she is.

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.442
She looks absolutely gorgeous.
-Little Freeya.

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:12.144
-And she's so beautiful.

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:14.247
You tried to get her
in the film?

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.415
-Seth, I tried everything.
-Yeah.

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:18.283
-Because this is
historical moment.

00:05:18.283 --> 00:05:19.485
-Yeah!
-I was like,

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:20.719
"I'm gonna get my baby
in this film.

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:22.622
It says there's a toddler.
They need a toddler.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.023
My baby's gonna be
the toddler."

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.324
-Yeah.
-We got her dressed,

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.159
we got her in hair and makeup.
-They were okay with it.

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:29.328
The director knew.
Everybody signed off.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:30.996
-Everybody.
We even got her --

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:32.564
like, you know,
you got to sign union papers.

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:34.267
-Yeah, exactly.
-She was excited.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:37.436
Miss Thing decided,
"It's nap time,

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.205
and I'm not here for it."
-Really?

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:42.441
-Yes, and she was supposed to go
into Fantasia's arms

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:43.676
at the end of the movie.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.712
And she said, when Fantasia
tried to get her,

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:47.513
"Don't touch me!
Please don't touch me!"

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.747
And I was like, "Oh, my God."

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:50.849
And as soon as that happened,
Blitz was like,

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:53.852
"Danielle, I'm sorry your baby
ain't gonna cut it.

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:55.454
She got to go."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:58.691
So, yeah, unfortunately,
my child is not in the movie.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.993
But we have a great story.
-Yeah, you have a great story.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:03.863
It's good to know that
there's always a backup child.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:05.431
-Always.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.900
-That might be a little older
than the toddler.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.302
-Exactly.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:12.405
-But we have a really
wonderful video for you.

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.606
So you took her to see
"Little Mermaid."

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:16.041
-Oh, my gosh,
I took her to see Halle Bailey

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:19.378
in "The Little Mermaid,"
and I saw that the trailer

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:22.515
was coming on,
so I had to get it on tape.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.817
And I got a video of my daughter

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:28.020
watching her mommy
in the trailer.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.323
-It's really a wonderful age
because when you watch this,

00:06:31.323 --> 00:06:33.125
she really can't wrap her head
around what's happening.

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:35.328
-No, she doesn't know.
She's four.

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:36.996
Now she's four.
She was three at the time.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:39.832
So, yeah, her first movie
that she's ever seen.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.467
And she got to see Mommy
in the trailer.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.669
-And the best thing about it
is she feels like

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.171
she's breaking news to you.
-Oh, my God.

00:06:46.171 --> 00:06:47.440
And to everybody
in the theater.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:51.477
-Yeah. Look at this
incredible video of Freeya.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:53.545 line:0%
-Oh, Miss Millie.

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:55.948 line:0%
Ain't got no kinfolk
around these parts.

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:58.784 line:0%
-That's you.

00:06:58.784 --> 00:07:02.254 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
-That's you. That's you.

00:07:02.254 --> 00:07:04.323 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:06.192 line:0%
Mommy!
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:09.495 line:0%
-Mommy.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:11.096
-Oh, are you trying
to make me cry?

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:13.365
-It's so good.
-You're trying to make me cry.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:17.269
-I -- It makes me cry.
Also, does she always dress

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:19.138
like that for the cinema?
-Yes.

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.540
-She does?
-As of today, she will be.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.175
-Yeah, but is that --
Like, I just --

00:07:23.175 --> 00:07:24.577
I was watching it
the second time.

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:25.978
I'm like, "Ah, she really
is wearing a tiara."

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:28.614
-I know, because -- Well,
they have all these outfits

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:30.015
at the store
for "Little Mermaid,"

00:07:30.015 --> 00:07:32.684
and it came with a tiara,
so I put her in tiara, yeah.

00:07:32.684 --> 00:07:35.588
She's in theme.
-She looked great,

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:37.222
and it was very sweet to watch.
Congratulations again.

00:07:37.222 --> 00:07:38.858
One more toast to you
and your nominations.

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:41.026
-Thank you. Thank you, friend.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:41.026 --> 00:07:43.495
-Danielle Brooks, everyone.
"The Color Purple"

00:07:43.495 --> 00:07:44.897
will be in theaters
December 25th.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.231
Stick around.
We'll be right back

00:07:46.231 --> 00:07:47.567
with music
from Alexander Stewart.

